Q: Foreground Service doesn&#39;t keep score of data A: <p>The timer's operation is based on coroutines. The timer was started - a new coroutine was launched (<code>scope.launch</code>). The timer was stopped, and the coroutine was canceled (<code>job?.cancel()</code>). And so it is every time. And the variables <code>hours</code>,<code>minutes</code> and <code>seconds</code> are the same. When you start the timer after a pause, 1 s passes before the first update of the values. It is at this moment that you see '0L' (the default value of the variables). Then, at the next <code>runStopwatch</code>, they are updated.</p>
<p>If you want the zero to disappear, insert <code>updateRunningState</code> in <code>resumeStopwatch </code>and resume the timer before the coroutine starts.</p>
<pre><code>    private fun resumeStopwatch(onTick: (contentText: String) -&gt; Unit) {
        // Cancel the coroutine which updates the sub-activity stopwatch
        job?.cancel()
        stopwatchSub.stop()

        // Cancel the sub-activity notification
        notificationManager.cancel(SUB_ACTIVITY_NOTIFICATION_ID)



            // Resume the main activity stopwatch and Update the stopwatch
            stopwatchMain.resume()
            stopwatchMain.updateRunningState()



        job = scope.launch {
            while (true) {
                runStopwatch(stopwatchMain, onTick)
                delay(1000)
            }
        }
    }
</code></pre>
<p>If I understood your second question correctly, then it's about</p>
<pre><code>Log.i(&quot;StopwatchService&quot;, &quot;formattedText $formattedText&quot;)
</code></pre>
<p>There's the same problem - there's no <code>hours</code>,<code>minutes</code> and <code>seconds </code>update. you need to reset their values in the <code>stop</code> method.</p>
<pre><code>    fun stop() {
        currentState = StopwatchState.Paused(0L)
        hours = 0L
        minutes = 0L
        seconds = 0L
    }
</code></pre>
<p>Otherwise the values will be updated only after 1 s at the next call to <code>updateRunningState</code>, and before that the timer will show 18 s</p>
